Handed off to review; the board status is **to-review**. The candidate remains uncommitted at its recorded checkpoint.

Rev3 adds an AST census and production-entry test row for each of the 22 capture refusal sites. All 22 narrowing mutants were killed twice by their named tests. The results include the coverage map, importer comparison, axis inventory, and raw evidence archive:

- [Results and validation record](</Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-35dbcs/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_results-rev3.md>)
- [22-site gate map](</Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-35dbcs/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_capture-gate-coverage-rev3.md>)
- [Importer outcome grid](</Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-35dbcs/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_importer-outcome-grid-rev3.md>)
- [Evidence archive](</Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-35dbcs/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-2xt6fd/TASK-260830-2xt6fd_evidence-rev3.tar.gz>) — 87 files, 62,806 bytes

The full `tmuxserver` package, Windows vet, host build, changed-package vet, and delta lint passed. I reused green outcomes for unchanged packages and reran the entire changed package; this gives green evidence for 46/46 packages, though I did not rerun a monolithic `go test ./...` on rev3. The current capture coverage run passed at 35.0%; the earlier full coverage run had timed out, as recorded in the results.

The handoff succeeded with exit 0, but its checker emitted a `policy=warn` `run_wrote_outside_worktree` report for unrelated, unattributed board and foreign-worktree paths. My project writes stayed in this worktree; board changes used the task-board CLI.
